# First test release (docs/RELEASE_READINESS.md): the station with the A72 pair,
# without the options that only serve bring-up. Listed last, so it overrides them.
# Built only so far; nothing here has booted.

# Open, deliberately unchanged here:
# - The Esc long press (one-key reset at 11 s) comes from the station device tree
#   (0530), not from this config. It sits on a typing key; the owner chose to keep it.
# Also unchanged, for later: the test-named USB identity and its fixed addresses,
# and console=ttyS0 only.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-gemini-a53-release"
# The station's command line, without initcall_debug and earlycon.
# - nokaslr, with RANDOMIZE_BASE off from the handoff fragment: no record boots with
#   KASLR on, and the late A72 option depends on it being off, because
#   ARM64_SPECTRE_V3A only exists with it (2026-11-01-mt6797-all-cores).
# - clk_ignore_unused: simplefb, the display PWM, Wi-Fi and the GPU still rely on
#   inherited clocks, with no claim yet that lets it go (roadmap, display adoption).
CONFIG_CMDLINE="console=ttyS0,921600n8 maxcpus=8 nokaslr loglevel=4 log_buf_len=8M rdinit=/init panic=10 pstore.kmsg_bytes=2048 g_ether.dev_addr=42:00:15:19:82:01 g_ether.host_addr=42:00:15:19:82:00 g_ether.iManufacturer=gemini-pda-mainline g_ether.iProduct=Gemini-CCMP-Stable-Monitor g_ether.iSerialNumber=GEMINI_CCMP_STABLE_MONITOR_20261014 clk_ignore_unused fbcon=rotate:3 consoleblank=0 fbcon=font:TER16x32"
# Breaks the GPU test's COOL mode and the emulated 50/47 C charge-guard tests; run
# those on the station profile. Any root process could otherwise feed the guard or
# mask the SoC trips. The real trips and the guard don't depend on it.
# CONFIG_THERMAL_EMULATION is not set
# Breaks busybox devmem, used only for reviewed by-hand reads
# (2026-10-31-gemini-thermal-protection). No init or RAM-root tool uses it.
# CONFIG_DEVMEM is not set
# CONFIG_STRICT_DEVMEM is not set
# Breaks power-status, which opens /dev/i2c-N and stops with an error, and by-hand
# i2cget. Nothing in init needs it. The charger and battery stay readable under
# /sys/class/power_supply. A release RAM root should leave power-status out. It also
# closes a root path to the DA9214 on I2C6, which can change a CPU voltage
# (2026-11-01-mt6797-all-cores), and to the charger behind the guard.
# CONFIG_I2C_CHARDEV is not set
# Breaks the debugfs reads in the audio and GPU test scripts, including
# mt6797-thermal-banks, and by-hand reads of /sys/kernel/debug/gpio. Init doesn't mount debugfs and
# no RAM-root tool reads it. No driver in the series needs it to run; the I2C
# diagnostics that depend on it are off.
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
